Subject: ps2xRuntime: VIF1 keeps decoding VIFcodes while a PATH2 IMAGE transfer is pending

An IMAGE GIFtag whose NLOOP runs past the end of its DIRECT payload left the interpreter consuming the
following VIF stream as raw image data. In a TTE chain the next bytes are the NOP/DIRECT VIFcodes from
the next DMAtag's upper half, so every texture or CLUT uploaded over several DIRECTs landed 8 bytes late
(Rule of Rose: location.tm2 matched the GS memory only at a +8 byte shift, its CLUT at 2 entries).

The pending IMAGE count is GIF state: it now continues only through DIRECT/DIRECTHL payloads. A transfer
that ends inside a DIRECT payload (normal-mode DMA, VIF1 FIFO writes) is tracked separately as VIF state
(m_vif1PendingDirectQwc) and its rest continues the same command in the next call.

